pmc:ChaosMagicKiaKaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kia: free will arising from the absence of causality in an amplified randomness"@en, "Kia: freier Wille aus der Abwesenheit von Kausalität in einer verstärkten Zufälligkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third part of the psychic anatomy, the Kia or spirit or Free Will, arises not from the presence of anything but from the absence of a certain thing: nervous systems amplify the random element present in all material events, and we interpret our partly random, chaotic and unpredictable behavior as free will and creativity. We can never perceive what lies at the center or centers of our free will, for there exists only the void of causality's absence, sparks of the chaos from which matter and ether co-evolve."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:LiberKaos ;
    dcterms:source "Carroll, Liber Kaos (Boston and York Beach: Weiser Books; first published 1992, printing of 2003), Liber Kaos, ch. 1 Principia Magica, Quantum Metaphysics, p. 26; read in a full-text layer whose running heads carry the page" .

pmc:ChaosMagicSpeciesResonance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resonance with an animal form accesses the pattern of its whole species"@en, "Resonanz mit einer Tierform erschließt das Muster ihrer ganzen Art"@de ;
    skos:definition "Achieving resonance with the etheric pattern of some animal form is to access the pattern of its species in general."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
